WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:08.130
Bill Duke, Actor/Filmmaker/Author: True story
and very few people knew this ever happened.

00:00:08.130 --> 00:00:19.310
I’m sitting at my monitor one day and the
assistant says “Do you know who is standing

00:00:19.310 --> 00:00:20.310
behind you?”

00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:22.500
I said “What are you talking about?”

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:23.500
“Gordon Parks.”

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:25.800
I said “Get out of here, I’m working.

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:26.800
Stop playing.”

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:29.770
He said “No, Gordon Parks is standing right
behind you.”

00:00:29.770 --> 00:00:31.990
He’s one of my heroes.

00:00:31.990 --> 00:00:37.760
So I turn around and he says “Don’t get
up, don’t get up.”

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:48.920
And he walks to me and he puts his hand on
my shoulder and he says “Never stop.”

00:00:48.920 --> 00:00:58.710
I just looked at him and…[is speechless].

00:00:58.710 --> 00:01:14.400
He walked away and I was like…you’re given
signs from the Universe you know and he was

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:20.990
one of the things that propelled me into continuing
because whenever you get depressed or something

00:01:20.990 --> 00:01:24.500
and you want to stop and you don’t stop
because of those people who came along and

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:28.160
said “Don’t you ever think of stopping.”

00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:34.100
Because I’m not going to lie to you there
are times I wanted to give up because it’s

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:37.800
like hard.

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:45.409
But then you think of the people who loved
you enough to encourage you, you don’t stop.

00:01:45.409 --> 00:01:52.420
And it’s also your family’s legacy.

00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:54.130
Could you justify stopping?

00:01:54.130 --> 00:01:55.710
Hell yeah!

00:01:55.710 --> 00:01:57.760
Is it unfair?

00:01:57.760 --> 00:01:58.760
Yes.

00:01:58.760 --> 00:02:01.500
If you don’t fit into certain boxes is it
prejudice?

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:02.520
Yes.

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:06.390
Are there people who don’t like you because
of the color of your skin?

00:02:06.390 --> 00:02:07.390
Yes.

00:02:07.390 --> 00:02:13.389
Are there people who don’t like you because
you are as smart as them?

00:02:13.389 --> 00:02:17.319
Yes.

00:02:17.319 --> 00:02:31.950
I mean if the boogeyman has got his foot on
your neck, you have one of two choices.

00:02:31.950 --> 00:02:45.989
He’s ten times bigger than you, he’s 15
foot tall and my neck is cracking, I might

00:02:45.989 --> 00:02:48.709
as well surrender.

00:02:48.709 --> 00:02:53.900
That’s one choice.

00:02:53.900 --> 00:03:06.219
Or…if his foot is in your mouth you can
bite his toe.

00:03:06.219 --> 00:03:14.959
I choose toe biting because you know what?

00:03:14.959 --> 00:03:19.689
The bogeyman’s toe taste good.

00:03:19.689 --> 00:03:20.689
It really does.

00:03:20.689 --> 00:03:26.109
It has those little…it’s meaty and chunky…[imitates
eating] it’s good.

00:03:26.109 --> 00:03:36.909
Film Courage: It’s a light snack.

00:03:36.909 --> 00:03:40.280
Has meditation helped you notice gratitude?

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:46.749
Because I think some people see signs that
do tell them to keep going and it sounds like

00:03:46.749 --> 00:03:53.549
you’ve taken certain things to heart and
know that this wasn’t just a coincidence

00:03:53.549 --> 00:03:56.350
or I was meant to hear this.

00:03:56.350 --> 00:03:58.969
I was meant to have this hand on my shoulder.

00:03:58.969 --> 00:04:03.639
I was meant to have someone take away my journal
in what seems like a bad thing and she reads

00:04:03.639 --> 00:04:09.400
it but then something great comes of it.

00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:17.070
Bill: Meditation saved my life.

00:04:17.070 --> 00:04:23.530
I was taught meditation (Transcendental Meditation
- TM) by a good friend of mine when I was

00:04:23.530 --> 00:04:33.030
in a Broadway play and doing very well but
I had gotten into substances because there

00:04:33.030 --> 00:04:43.930
are times in which the struggle is so difficult,
I was working and challenges and I just overloaded.

00:04:43.930 --> 00:04:56.740
And I ended up at a point where in a Broadway
play I’d be late to work and they told me

00:04:56.740 --> 00:04:58.390
“Don’t be late anymore.”

00:04:58.390 --> 00:05:11.530
And I came late again and they said your understudy
is going in and I got pissed off and my friend

00:05:11.530 --> 00:05:14.540
who saw this said “Bill, you’re sinking
fast.

00:05:14.540 --> 00:05:15.870
You have to do something.”

00:05:15.870 --> 00:05:17.290
I said “Like what?”

00:05:17.290 --> 00:05:21.480
See says “I know you like the drugs and
alcohol but try meditation.”

00:05:21.480 --> 00:05:24.320
I said “Those whoo-whoo people.

00:05:24.320 --> 00:05:26.600
Get out of here.”

00:05:26.600 --> 00:05:33.160
So it got worse and then she said “Try it.”

00:05:33.160 --> 00:05:37.440
Okay, I’ll try it.

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:40.080
So I tried it a couple of times, it was interesting
but I was still taking substances.

00:05:40.080 --> 00:05:48.070
And then after awhile she said “I’ll tell
you what, I’ll make you a deal.”

00:05:48.070 --> 00:05:59.470
She said “If you meditate for six weeks
without taking any substances of any kind

00:05:59.470 --> 00:06:07.640
and if you still want substances after six
weeks, I’ll buy you an ounce of anything

00:06:07.640 --> 00:06:09.190
you want.”

00:06:09.190 --> 00:06:14.830
And I’m thinking “Boy!

00:06:14.830 --> 00:06:15.920
An ounce of anything I want?

00:06:15.920 --> 00:06:17.210
Are you kidding me?

00:06:17.210 --> 00:06:19.480
I’ll take this bet with you.”

00:06:19.480 --> 00:06:23.870
I just knew it wasn’t going to work.

00:06:23.870 --> 00:06:38.560
The first two weeks I felt something like…more
ease, less stress.

00:06:38.560 --> 00:06:49.400
Second and third week, more focus.

00:06:49.400 --> 00:06:58.500
Fourth and fifth week, the peace that I was
getting out of the substances, I was

00:06:58.500 --> 00:07:01.470
getting through meditation and more.

00:07:01.470 --> 00:07:11.780
I was getting a deeper sense of something
I can’t even explain.

00:07:11.780 --> 00:07:18.110
I haven’t touched substances since that
day and that was in 1974.

00:07:18.110 --> 00:07:21.600
I became a TM teacher.

00:07:21.600 --> 00:07:24.010
It’s changed my life too.

00:07:24.010 --> 00:07:32.940
I can’t even tell you, it’s hard to explain.

00:07:32.940 --> 00:07:38.270
I could tell you more stories about what I’ve
been through but that was God working again

00:07:38.270 --> 00:07:39.500
showing me Transcendental Meditation.

00:07:39.500 --> 00:07:42.250
It changed my life for my own salvation.

00:07:42.250 --> 00:07:49.810
The lady who asked me to turn around and Miss
Walker and Dr. Hall, its…I recognize these

00:07:49.810 --> 00:07:57.080
things and people are going to think I’m
crazy because “God is doing this.”

00:07:57.080 --> 00:07:59.840
“What does your God look like?”

00:07:59.840 --> 00:08:00.840
“I don’t know?

00:08:00.840 --> 00:08:04.550
I know he is there.

00:08:04.550 --> 00:08:09.490
I trust because there are things that have
happened that I know.”

00:08:09.490 --> 00:08:13.990
I’ll give you another example, it’s in
my book.

